  "body": "Answering \"does the Analytics search box actually work?\" — it worked, but it was looking at a minority of what it had stored.\n\n## The gap, measured on real data\n\nSearch matched only `input_text` and `output_text`. On the reporter's live log:\n\n```\nrows                50,059\nwith thinking_text  27,745  (55.4%)\nwith tool_calls     38,934  (77.8%)\n```\n\nProven by probing 600 of their real requests — a phrase occurring **only** in reasoning and one occurring **only** in a tool call:\n\n| | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `\"understand what keys\"` (reasoning only) | **0 rows** | 308 |\n| `\"backend start command\"` (tool call only) | **0 rows** | 422 |\n| control: phrase from the prompt | 600 | 600 |\n\n## What changed\n\n- Search covers **prompt, reply, reasoning, and tool calls**.\n- Tool calls match on their **string values**, not their JSON encoding — the encoding both misses (`C:\\Users` is stored escaped) and misleads (every row contains the key name `command`).\n- **Multi-word queries require every word somewhere in the request**, not an adjacent phrase. `proxy 8082` now finds a request whose prompt says \"restart the proxy\" and whose reasoning says \"port 8082 is busy\". A single word is unchanged, and since a phrase match implies every word is present, this only ever adds results.\n\n## Performance\n\nSearching two more fields costs less than the version that searched two:\n\n| 600 real rows | first working version | this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| three words | 991 ms | **518 ms** |\n| tool path | 1,116 ms | **436 ms** |\n\nCase folding moved from Python text to bytes: 7× cheaper on a 43 KB body (0.533 → 0.073 ms), found by profiling the per-row cost. It is also **more correct** — SQLite's `LIKE` is case-insensitive for ASCII only, so folding in text would have made compressed rows match things the inline rows beside them did not.\n\n## Verification\n\n- A parametrised fixture runs the same assertions against **both** storage forms, so inline and compressed cannot drift.\n- Driven in a real browser against a server serving 600 real requests: the card reads 308 / 334 / 0 / 600 for reasoning-only, tool-call-only, nonsense and cleared, rows render, no console errors.\n- One pre-existing test was asserting the old phrase semantics (`\"failure in module 0\"` now legitimately matches `10`, `20`, `100`…) and was rewritten to test what it was for.\n- Docs contract tests now fail if the README, USAGE or Guide stop saying what search covers, or if the search box placeholder stops saying it.\n\nLocal suite 3,405 passed, with the 6 known PowerShell installer failures that predate this branch.\n\nMINOR: 4.45.1 → 4.46.0.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
